From 88d2ddb9e116b13a291f2661c24de9a26c3a4d78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bjorn Pagen <11238136+bjornpagen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:29:04 -0600
Subject: [PATCH v1] Use per-tuple context for the key columns in
 ExecUpdateLockMode

ExecUpdateLockMode() reads the relation's key columns with
RelationGetIndexAttrBitmap(), which returns a fresh copy of the bitmap
in CurrentMemoryContext.  Its callers, ExecBRUpdateTriggers(),
ExecOnConflictUpdate() and ExecMergeMatched(), call it once per row
with the long-lived ExecutorState current, so the copies pile up until
the end of the query: about 40 bytes per row, 400MB for an INSERT ...
ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE that updates 10 million rows, and as much for an
UPDATE of as many rows of a table with any BEFORE ROW UPDATE trigger,
even a disabled one.

Commit f24523672de moved the other bitmap this function builds, the
result of ExecGetAllUpdatedCols(), into the per-tuple context.  The
key-column copy showed up in the profile posted to the same thread, but
was left out.  Build it in the per-tuple context too; nothing uses it
past the function.

The leak dates back to 0ac5ad5134f, which introduced the key-column
lock modes.  Backpatch to all supported branches.

Reported-by: REPLACE-ME <REPLACE-ME>
Discussion: https://postgr.es/m/222a3442-7f7d-246c-ed9b-a76209d19239@enterprisedb.com
Backpatch-through: 15
---
 src/backend/executor/execMain.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/backend/executor/execMain.c b/src/backend/executor/execMain.c
index cfe1c2a801b..3412dca12fb 100644
--- a/src/backend/executor/execMain.c
+++ b/src/backend/executor/execMain.c
@@ -2596,15 +2596,22 @@ ExecUpdateLockMode(EState *estate, ResultRelInfo *relinfo)
 {
 	Bitmapset  *keyCols;
 	Bitmapset  *updatedCols;
+	MemoryContext oldcxt;
 
 	/*
 	 * Compute lock mode to use.  If columns that are part of the key have not
 	 * been modified, then we can use a weaker lock, allowing for better
 	 * concurrency.
+	 *
+	 * Callers do this once per row, so build the bitmap of key columns, which
+	 * RelationGetIndexAttrBitmap returns as a fresh copy, in the per-tuple
+	 * context, as ExecGetAllUpdatedCols does with the updated columns.
 	 */
 	updatedCols = ExecGetAllUpdatedCols(relinfo, estate);
+	oldcxt = MemoryContextSwitchTo(GetPerTupleMemoryContext(estate));
 	keyCols = RelationGetIndexAttrBitmap(relinfo->ri_RelationDesc,
 										 INDEX_ATTR_BITMAP_KEY);
+	MemoryContextSwitchTo(oldcxt);
 
 	if (bms_overlap(keyCols, updatedCols))
 		return LockTupleExclusive;
